From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 10:47:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): intense text is brightened, not emboldened
 (KD-13)

WT's intenseTextStyle is two switches and neither reached the engine, so
`top` beside a cascadia pane showed the difference twice over: cascadia
lifted its intense headers to bright white where ghostty left them the
plain foreground, and ghostty drew them with a bold face where cascadia
- whose default is bright, and *not* bold - drew regular strokes.

The colour half is not `bold-color = bright` on its own. That lifts a
palette colour to its bright twin, and text in the default foreground
has no index to lift, which is most of a `top` screen; measured, it
changed nothing. Cascadia's own rule looks the default foreground up in
the dark half of the palette and uses the bright entry it matches, so
the translator does that lookup and names the colour outright - which
also turns the rest of the bold colours bright, covering both halves of
the rule in one entry.

The face half is `font-style-bold = false`, ghostty's spelling for a
disabled style, which falls back to the regular face.

Measured on one capture of two panes on one profile: bold text is
#F2F2F2 in both, `1;31` is the scheme's brightRed #BA3A45 in both, and
the bold row carries the plain row's stroke weight in both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
